em_assets/steam/apps/256714789/movie.293x165.jpg?t=1526313608","hls":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/334940/159279/b1f18654a86f22c6d0cd08dfa36e832572fca448/1750510177/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1526313608","mp4":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/256714789/movie480.mp4"}],"genres":["Adventure","Indie"],"features":["Single-player","Steam Achievements","Steam Cloud","Remote Play on TV","Steam Trading Cards","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"controller":"full","dev":["Villa Gorilla"],"pub":["Team17 Digital Ltd"],"released":"May 29, 2018","meta":84,"langs":["English","French","Italian","German","Spanish - Spain","Russian","Simplified Chinese","Japanese","Korean"],"min":[["OS","Windows 7"],["Processor","Intel i3-2100 @ 3GHz / AMD A8-5500 @ 3.2GHz"],["Memory","4 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GT 630 1GB / AMD Radeon 7770 1GB / Intel HD 530"],["DirectX","Version 10"],["Storage","3 GB available space"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Yoku arrives on the tropical island of Mokumana hoping for an easy life delivering parcels, only to find that the island's ancient deity is caught in a troubled slumber. He becomes the local postman, rebuilds the post office and travels about by being flipped and bumped around like a pinball, mixing pinball mechanics with platforming and exploration.\n\nThe hand-painted island is non-linear, with several questlines that can be tackled in any order you like. The tone is bright and playful, and the pinball-platformer idea gives it a distinct feel. It is single-player with full controller support, and it suits players who enjoy colourful exploration games built around an unusual mechanic."}}